# rhwp HFT quote width, picture band spacing and print fill fixes for why-hwp, measured against Hangul 2024 output.
# Base: rhwp 7213ed1f9 after the source edits in wasm/patch-rhwp.sh and
# wasm/patches/rhwp-layout.patch, rhwp-layout2.patch, rhwp-layout3.patch,
# rhwp-layout4.patch and rhwp-layout5.patch; apply this after
# rhwp-layout5.patch.
# Zero-context diff (apply with git apply --unidiff-zero).
#
# - font_metrics_overlays.rs: the plain 한양중고딕 (Hanyang Junggothic) HFT
#   double quotes U+201C and U+201D advance 375/1000 em, the width in the
#   font's own advance table and in the Type 3 font Hangul 2024 prints. They
#   were measured as half of the substitute font's full-width glyph (0.5 em),
#   which pushed the rest of the line 0.125 em right per quote.
# - float_placement.rs, layout.rs: when an empty paragraph holds one
#   top-and-bottom picture anchored to it and the picture's band takes the
#   paragraph's own line (stored segment width 0), Hangul puts the first line
#   of the next paragraph at the band's bottom; that paragraph's spacing before
#   is spent inside the band. The spacing was added below the band a second
#   time. It is taken back only when the next paragraph's stored first line
#   sits at the band's bottom, so documents without stored lines, or with a
#   stored line elsewhere, lay out as before.
# - document_core/queries/rendering.rs, paint/builder.rs: in a print (PDF)
#   render, glyphs of a declared HFT font are projected through the precise
#   device matrix of Hangul's printer (on A4 a 0.99946 x 0.99891 scale on each
#   glyph group) until the document paints its first solid fill. Which
#   rectangles count as that fill now always follows Hangul 2024, where a table
#   cell or paragraph background counts. It followed the document's
#   compatibility generation, and under the older rule a document whose only
#   fills are such backgrounds kept the scale on every later page, which
#   Hangul 2024 does not print.
# - layout/text_measurement.rs and float_placement.rs cover the quote width
#   and the band spacing.
